# Trivy Vulnerability Ignore File
# This file contains vulnerabilities that are being intentionally ignored
# Each entry should include a comment explaining why it's safe to ignore

# ==================== POLICY ====================
# GitHub workflows enforce: CRITICAL,HIGH severity only
# See: .github/actions/trivy-scan/action.yml
#
# MEDIUM and LOW severity vulnerabilities do not block CI/CD and
# should NOT be added to this file unless there is a specific reason
# to suppress them from local development scans.

# ==================== EXAMPLE FORMAT ====================
# CVE-YYYY-XXXXX - Brief description
# Affects: package-name version
# Severity: CRITICAL/HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW
# Issue: Detailed description of vulnerability
# Risk: Analysis of actual risk in this context
# Status: Fixed in version X.Y.Z / No fix available (affected)
# Reason: Why it's safe to ignore (false positive, not applicable, etc.)
# Review: When to re-evaluate this decision
# CVE-YYYY-XXXXX

# ==================== ACTIVE IGNORES ====================

# CVE-2024-52308 - GitHub CLI SSH command injection vulnerability (FALSE POSITIVE)
# Affects: github.com/cli/cli/v2
# Severity: HIGH
# Issue: RCE via malicious Codespace SSH server when using `gh codespace ssh` or `gh codespace logs`
#        Improper validation of remote username allows command injection via SSH arguments
# Risk: This container installs gh CLI v2.83.0 (see Dockerfile line 19: ARG GH_VERSION=2.83.0)
#       CVE-2024-52308 was fixed in gh CLI v2.62.0 (released 2024-11-14)
#       Version 2.83.0 > 2.62.0, therefore not vulnerable
# Status: Fixed in version 2.62.0 (we're running 2.83.0)
# Reason: False positive - Trivy incorrectly identifies gh v2.83.0 as vulnerable
#         Possible issue: Trivy's version detection for Go binaries or stale vulnerability DB
# Review: Remove this entry when Trivy's vulnerability database is updated to correctly
#         recognize gh v2.83.0 as not vulnerable. Check Trivy release notes and test without
#         this ignore after Trivy updates. Next review: 2026-01-01
CVE-2024-52308

